e","k":"parameter","d":"Measured incident spectrum, used to normalise by wavelength"},{"t":"cuttofmax","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-cuttofmax","k":"parameter","d":"Time-of-flight window kept, in \u00b5s; a narrow window approximates a monochromatic beam"},{"t":"cuttofmin","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-cuttofmin","k":"parameter","d":"Time-of-flight window kept, in \u00b5s; a narrow window approximates a monochromatic beam"},{"t":"darkfilename","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-darkfilename","k":"parameter","d":"Dark-current run subtracted as instrumental background"},{"t":"detectoroffset","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-detectoroffset","k":"parameter","d":"Detector position offset along the beam, mm \u2014 from AgBe calibration"},{"t":"fitinelasticincoh","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-fitinelasticincoh","k":"parameter","d":"Whether to fit and remove incoherent inelastic scattering"},{"t":"incohfit_qmax","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-incohfit-qmax","k":"parameter","d":"Q window that fit uses; must lie inside the configuration's range (CFG-02)"},{"t":"incohfit_qmin","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-incohfit-qmin","k":"parameter","d":"Q window that fit uses; must lie inside the configuration's range (CFG-02)"},{"t":"maskfilename","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-maskfilename","k":"parameter","d":"Detector mask applied to every run in the configuration"},{"t":"numqbins","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-numqbins","k":"parameter","d":"Number of bins in the 1D I(Q)"},{"t":"numqxqybins","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-numqxqybins","k":"parameter","d":"Bins per axis in the 2D I(Qx,Qy)"},{"t":"outputwavelengthdependentprofile","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-outputwavelengthdependentprofile","k":"parameter","d":"Also write I(Q) per wavelength bin"},{"t":"qbintype","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-qbintype","k":"parameter","d":"`log` | log binning for I(Q)"},{"t":"qmax","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-qmax","k":"parameter","d":"Q range kept in the 1D profile"},{"t":"qmin","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-qmin","k":"parameter","d":"Q range kept in the 1D profile"},{"t":"sampleaperturesize","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-sampleaperturesize","k":"parameter","d":"10 | default unless the experiment specifies otherwise"},{"t":"sampleoffset","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-sampleoffset","k":"parameter","d":"Sample position offset along the beam, mm \u2014 from AgBe calibration"},{"t":"scalecomponents.detector1","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-scalecomponentsdetector1","k":"parameter","d":"`[x, y, z]` scale of the detector geometry \u2014 from AgBe calibration"},{"t":"selectminincoh","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-selectminincoh","k":"parameter","d":"True | only consulted when `fitinelasticincoh` is on"},{"t":"sensitivityfilename","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-sensitivityfilename","k":"parameter","d":"Flood map correcting pixel-to-pixel response"},{"t":"standardabsolutescale","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-standardabsolutescale","k":"parameter","d":"Factor putting the reduced intensity on an absolute scale, from a standard measured in that same configuration (SCL-02)"},{"t":"timesliceinterval","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-timesliceinterval","k":"parameter","d":"Split a run into time slices, and how long each slice is"},{"t":"useerrorweighting","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-useerrorweighting","k":"parameter","d":"True | usually on; see the 2.5 m note below"},{"t":"usemaskbacktubes","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-usemaskbacktubes","k":"parameter","d":"Mask the back tube bank as well"},{"t":"usetimeslice","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-usetimeslice","k":"parameter","d":"Split a run into time slices, and how long each slice is"},{"t":"wavelengthstep","p":"parameters.html","a":"param-wavelengthstep","k":"parameter","d":"0.1 | used for every configuration"},{"t":"Where a value comes from","p":"parameters.html","a":"where-a-value-comes-from","k":"page","d":"Parameters"},{"t":"How a parameter reaches the reduction","p":"parameters.html","a":"how-a-parameter-reaches-the-reduction","k":"page","d":"Parameters"},{"t":"BKG-01","p":"protocol.html","a":"rule-BKG-01","k":"rule","d":"The background run is from the same configuration as the row it serves."},{"t":"BKG-02","p":"protocol.html","a":"rule-BKG-02","k":"rule","d":"A row's background is not the row's own scattering run."},{"t":"BKG-03","p":"protocol.html","a":"rule-BKG-03","k":"rule","d":"All non-background rows in an experiment use the *same* background sample unless"},{"t":"CAL-01","p":"protocol.html","a":"rule-CAL-01","k":"rule","d":"Every referenced mask, flood, dark and flux file exists and is non-empty."},{"t":"CAL-02","p":"protocol.html","a":"rule-CAL-02","k":"rule","d":"The flood (sensitivity) matches the detector distance: 1.3 m \u2192 `1o3m`,"},{"t":"CAL-03","p":"protocol.html","a":"rule-CAL-03","k":"rule","d":"Mask, flood, dark, flux and the AgBe offsets come from one cycle, chosen by run"},{"t":"CAL-04","p":"protocol.html","a":"rule-CAL-04","k":"rule","d":"A mask is never taken from another IPTS's shared folder: those are frequently"},{"t":"CAL-05","p":"protocol.html","a":"rule-CAL-05","k":"rule","d":"Detector offset, scale components and sample offset are only meaningful if an"},{"t":"CAT-01","p":"protocol.html","a":"rule-CAT-01","k":"rule","d":"Every run carries a `run_class` before matching: `scattering`, `transmission`,"},{"t":"CAT-02","p":"protocol.html","a":"rule-CAT-02","k":"rule","d":"Each configuration that has scattering runs must also have an `empty_trans` run"},{"t":"CAT-03","p":"protocol.html","a":"rule-CAT-03","k":"rule","d":"More than one `empty_trans` in a configuration means a choice was made silently."},{"t":"CAT-04","p":"protocol.html","a":"rule-CAT-04","k":"rule","d":"Same for more than one `bkg_scatt` per configuration."},{"t":"CAT-05","p":"protocol.html","a":"rule-CAT-05","k":"rule","d":"Background keywords are tested **before** the empty-beam pattern, so"},{"t":"CAT-06","p":"protocol.html","a":"